# debug.keystore — the pinned DEBUG signing key

Every CI build signs the debug APK with this key (copied to
~/.android/debug.keystore before Gradle runs), so each new build installs
as an *update* over the last one instead of demanding an uninstall.
Without it, every CI machine mints its own throwaway debug key and
Android refuses the "update".

Debug-only, on purpose:
- The credentials are the Android-standard debug ones
  (alias `androiddebugkey`, password `android`) — this key proves
  "same builder", not identity. It must NEVER sign a Play Store release;
  the release keystore (Phase E) stays secret and out of this repo.
- Committing a debug key to a public repo is the accepted tradeoff for a
  dev channel: anyone could sign an APK with it, which is exactly why it
  must never be the release key.

Regenerating it would break update-installs for everyone on the old key
(one reinstall), so don't.
